	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "neuloTauNnp9mjRU8",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 35, DX 11, IQ 11, HT 13, HP 35, WILL 13, PER 13, FP 13, SPEED 6, MOVE 12, DODGE 9, DR 6. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "nVNT_sTwgLXRh3K6q",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 79 (offense 39, protection 40), threat tier major, appearing 1."
		},
		{
			"id": "nRlThNBRCKq25jZ5m",
			"text": "Acid Breath: Acid Breath (13): 6d corrosion, Reach Ranged, cone. A cone of acid that catches everything in front of the dragon. It costs the creature to use and cannot be repeated every second, which is the only reason a fight with one lasts more than a turn."
		},
		{
			"id": "nU2TrNrVBvEQxOY-U",
			"text": "Frightful Presence: No attack roll and no active defense. Frightful Presence: Reach Ranged, 20. Everyone who can see the dragon rolls Will. On a failure they are frightened of it and cannot willingly close, and a bad failure means they run. No attack roll and no defense; it costs the dragon nothing."
		},
		{
			"id": "neTIlo1qW_ExyNM10",
			"text": "Racial cost: 482 points of traits plus 18 points of skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "n6CUOL-r2YU8aOGeI",
			"text": "Body weight: 2,600 lb."
		},
		{
			"id": "naJG8iUUVbROrrlmN",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 4; air Move 12, 24 at a sprint (primary)."
		},
		{
			"id": "n_lofIfKagKI-w2tU",
			"text": "Immunity to its own element covers that one damage type and nothing else, and it is not in the published DR. A red dragon is not armored against a sword by being immune to fire."
		},
		{
			"id": "nf9yUPXdhrIktnY7r",
			"text": "The breath costs the creature to use and cannot be repeated every second, and a dragon that could breathe every turn would be a different fight. The published rating does not yet discount it for that, so it runs high for the sixteen colors whose breath is their best attack, worst for the acid breathers. Read these dragons as somewhat less dangerous than the number says."
		},
		{
			"id": "nyUHW0eiybLbdNodI",
			"text": "Monster statistics, ratings and description prose by Monsters on Automatic; AI-generated first draft, project-reviewed, released under CC BY 4.0."
		}
	],
